# Value files work identically under plain, MAC and enciphered comm settings
# when the session is not authenticated, LimitedCredit honours the
# limited-credit flag, and Commit/AbortTransaction reject any payload.
#
# Generated from tests/test_dfc_virtual_picc_value_vectors.c (/comm-limited-options) by
# recording the exchanges the reference engine performed, then
# cross-checked: all 26 byte expectations asserted by that test matched
# the recording exactly.
#
# Every file here has free access rights (0xEEEE), so the 0x9D on file 0x0E is
# LimitedCredit being refused on a file created without the limited-credit
# flag. That is a wrong-operation refusal, not an access-rights one, so it
# stayed 0x9D when access-rights refusals moved to 0xAE.

